{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Because you did not believe in Me.</b> Scripture revealed that had it not been for this sin alone, they would have entered the Land — so that one should not say of them: the sin of the wilderness generation, against which it was decreed that they would not enter, so too was the sin of Moses and Aaron. But is not ״הֲצֹאן וּבָקָר יִשָּׁחֵט״ (Numbers 11:22) more severe than this? Rather, because that was in private, Scripture spared him; but here, where it was in the presence of all Israel, Scripture did not spare him, on account of the sanctification of the Name." "<b>To sanctify Me.</b> For had you spoken to the rock and it had brought forth, I would have been sanctified in the eyes of the congregation, and they would say: this rock, which does not speak and does not hear and needs no sustenance, fulfills the word of the Omnipresent — all the more so we." "<b>Therefore you shall not bring.</b> By an oath, as in ״וְלָכֵן נִשְׁבַּעְתִּי לְבֵית עֵלִי״ (I Samuel 3) — He swore by an irrevocable decree that they would not prolong prayer over this."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:44.456134845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}